WEBVTT

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.180
Hey, get up, Dante!

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.800
What time is it?

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:28.410
I'm sorry I'm late for our meeting.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.790
Our client's train broke down along the way.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:40.630
--Tony...
--Huh?

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:46.930
It's me, Earnest. Don't you remember me?

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:51.120
How do you remember
someone you've never met before?

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:55.680
Just the way you speak,
you're Tony, all right.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:56.640
No doubt about it.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:00:57.970
Huh?

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.060
I can understand why you'd
rather not remember all of that.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.610
That was a terrible event...

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:07.970
But at last, I can clear
you and your mother's names!

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:10.510
I found evidence!

00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:14.140
Evidence that it was all caused by a devil!

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.340
There you go.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:00.060
Really... What is all this about?

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:09.530
You were late, and then
what you brought wasn't a job...

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:13.760
And what the heck was that guy talking about?

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:14.990
I thought you'd be interested.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.660
Well, when he's saying a
bunch of stuff like that...

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.510
Twenty years ago, in a small
port town called Morris Island,

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.660
there was a fire that
wiped out the whole town.

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.050
The majority of the townspeople died
in the fire, leaving only a few survivors.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:40.310
But afterwards, some of the
survivors gave testimonials saying

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:44.630
that an army of devils had attacked
the town before the fire broke out.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:52.100
But nobody would believe their stories.

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:53.350
I suppose not...

00:03:53.890 --> 00:03:56.530
That guy who was here
was one of those survivors.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.320
As was this "Tony"?

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:00.780
And his mother.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.100
So what was the whole
"clearing their names" thing about?

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:08.060
People said Tony's mother was
responsible for setting that fire.

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:10.380
She was apparently treated
pretty badly because of that.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.640
So, what ended up happening to that mother?

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.810
She took young Tony and
they fled from the town.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:21.060
And he thinks I was this Tony?

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:27.560
Ridiculous. What would make you
think that I could be this "Tony"?

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.470
I got a phone call.

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:32.600
Someone saying "I want you to arrange a
meeting for me with Tony the Devil Hunter."

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:37.600
You're the only devil hunter that I know...

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:46.970
Dante, are you sure the name
"Tony" doesn't ring any bells for you?

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:01.390
Welcome home, Tony.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.500
Morrison called me.

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.140
So you've come back to us.

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.310
That's not really what I'm doing--

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:12.450
I know.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.100
I'm still glad that you've come.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.700
Come on. It's this way.

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:31.200
I've said it before, but I'm not Tony.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.170
I can understand wanting to keep
your name on the down-low here.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.790
But you don't have anything to worry about.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:44.090
There aren't many left here that
know what happened 20 years ago.

00:05:45.740 --> 00:05:47.930
So much so that I get treated as an eccentric

00:05:47.930 --> 00:05:51.350
for still wanting to clarify
what really happened.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:54.540
I don't care one way or
the other. Who was it?

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:55.060
Huh?

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.280
Who was it that you heard about me from?

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:01.310
Very few people know
what it is that I actually do.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:04.220
Oh... You mean about being a devil hunter?

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:07.270
I just happened to hear about it
from a guy in one of the circus tents.

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:10.740
All right, take me to that circus tent.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:11.570
Huh?

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:16.610
Okay, then.

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:53.890
Of course, it's you.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.660
Is that the game you want to play?

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:21.820
Why would you pull a gun here?

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:24.370
Just saying a little "hello."

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:28.310
You've really toughened up.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:32.720
It looks like the circus is on holiday today.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:33.830
Let's go!

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:38.830
Our teacher will be so happy to see you.

00:07:38.830 --> 00:07:40.210
Teacher?

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:54.140
If you wanna play, you
come looking for me yourself.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:15.860
Ms. Margaret,

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:17.700
Tony's here!

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:19.400
Tony!

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.890
No, this guy's just calling me that.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:26.870
It seems like Tony doesn't want
anyone to know who he really is.

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:31.120
Can you blame him?
So, how is your mother doing?

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:34.930
She's dead. She's been dead for a long time.

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:36.850
Is that so? I'm sorry to hear that.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:41.470
I wished back then that I
could have helped your mother

00:08:41.470 --> 00:08:46.040
rid herself of some of the
suffering and sadness she endured.

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:52.110
Teacher, he works as a
devil hunter at present.

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:56.320
I see. You've really come a long
way, haven't you, Tony? Good for you.

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:01.680
Teacher... It's fine, isn't it?
We can tell Tony now, can't we?

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:05.250
Of course, that's why we
had him come here, after all.

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:11.640
This is to atone for making you and
your mother suffer so much back then.

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:13.100
What are you talking about?

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:17.390
I told you before.
That I finally found evidence!

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:21.720
Evidence that the destruction of our town
was not caused by a person, but by a devil!

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.200
--Ruins?
--Yes.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:38.050
You're not planning to summon
the devil from those ruins, are you?

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:41.250
You're good. You see through my whole plan.

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:44.600
Did the guy in the circus
tent tell you about that, too?

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:49.900
The meaning of the ruins,
how to summon the devil...

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:53.060
The guy who gave you the idea
that I'm Tony told you everything.

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:58.760
What's wrong with that?
I really did get to see you, after all.

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:02.860
The important thing is clearing
you and your mother's names.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:13.060
Brings back memories, doesn't it?

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:17.190
Well, this toast's a little delayed,
but here's to seeing you again.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:24.640
Oh, you're back?

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:25.320
Welcome home.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.670
Let me introduce you. This is my wife, Elise.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:34.220
He's a lot bigger than you
made him out to be in your stories.

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:36.010
Well, of course he is.

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:41.100
All my stories are from back
when we were kids. Really...

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:43.340
Oh, I guess you're right. Sorry.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:46.470
Oh, and I'll start preparing dinner.

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.440
You don't have to do that right now.
You just got back from work.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:50.680
But...

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:54.150
Why don't you just stay here
and have a chat with Tony, okay?

00:10:57.350 --> 00:11:01.960
You'll have to forgive me. This is the
first time I've met one of Earnest's friends...

00:11:02.360 --> 00:11:05.880
You don't have to worry
about me. I'm used to being alone.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:25.880
Everyone in this town
says that Earnest is eccentric.

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:30.680
Even his students call him strange.

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:35.600
Even after all the work he's done to
emulate Ms. Margaret and become a teacher.

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.200
What do you think?

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:42.890
Me, I wish he would just forget the past.

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.540
So tell him that.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.150
I have... I don't know how many times.

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:51.510
The truth is, even he was
on the verge of giving up.

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:53.990
Ms. Margaret has fallen sick and all...

00:11:54.790 --> 00:11:58.190
But then one day he came home ecstatic,

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:01.530
saying that he could clear up that
event that happened 20 years ago

00:12:02.740 --> 00:12:05.420
and that he would be able to meet you.

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:09.730
In his mind, you are something special.

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:14.640
I've heard so many stories
about you from him.

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:18.260
Always saying "Tony is
the most wonderful guy"...

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:19.730
Once he starts talking about you,

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:21.690
he could go on all night long
and still have more to tell.

00:12:21.980 --> 00:12:25.120
I know everything there is to know about you.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:29.890
Oh, wait. There is one
thing I don't know about you.

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:31.720
The promise you two made...

00:12:31.720 --> 00:12:32.510
Promise?

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:36.170
Yes. He says, "There's no way I
can break a promise with Tony,"

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:38.680
so the only thing he won't tell
me even now is the location

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:40.870
of that treasure box you two buried together.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:43.590
You know how kids think,

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:46.920
it's probably hidden somewhere
right in front of your eyes.

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:56.980
So you really aren't...

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:08.720
Please... Even if it's just while
you're in town, pretend to be Tony.

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:40.100
L-Long time, no see!

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:44.480
I went to the trouble to
see you in the afternoon,

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:45.780
but your manners are sadly lacking.

00:13:45.780 --> 00:13:49.350
I thought about saying something,
but by then you were gone.

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:50.730
What could I do?

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:55.300
Well, shall we get right down to
business and pick up where we left off?

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:58.130
Easy, easy, easy... hold your horses...

00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:01.500
I did this for your benefit.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:05.720
That old woman and young guy
have been snooping around the ruins...

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:13.510
I thought, "Boy, this is dangerous," so
I very nicely had the brat call you over.

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:15.560
So if you've got the motivation,

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:20.200
why not just take care of that
dangerous devil at the ruins yourself?

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:26.170
That's crazy talk! I make it a
point to only fight weaklings.

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:29.780
If this doesn't concern you at
all, you could've just not come.

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:33.160
I just wanted to see your face one last time!

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.130
You're so scary...

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:44.580
In the end, you were drawn here
by the smell of a devil, weren't you?

00:14:56.930 --> 00:14:59.640
Tony, you sure are an
early riser, aren't you?

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:01.810
I'll put some coffee on.

00:15:01.810 --> 00:15:04.980
Don't do it. Don't try to summon that devil.

00:15:07.080 --> 00:15:08.260
What are you saying?

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:11.000
What are you planning to do if
you're actually able to summon the devil?

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:15.680
If humans were capable of defeating them,

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.330
that tragedy 20 years ago
never would've happened.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:21.820
Or have you been relying
on me from the beginning?

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:24.640
I have no intention of asking for your help.

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:26.350
Don't play tougher than you are.

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:28.320
I can lower my fees for you if need be.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.180
I've made preparations.

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:35.520
That thing won't even
serve as a security blanket.

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:38.810
Does Elise have any idea
what you're planning to do?

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:40.260
This has nothing to do with her.

00:15:41.510 --> 00:15:46.110
You have to understand, Tony!
This problem concerns me too!

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:56.010
That's Tony, isn't it?

00:15:58.340 --> 00:15:59.600
How do you know?

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:01.540
You were just here yesterday.

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:03.720
You came alone today?

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:04.750
He's at school.

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:06.030
I see...

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:09.210
Tell me where those ruins are.

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:10.190
Hmm?

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:15.760
Earnest is planning on summoning that devil.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:19.560
He wants to clear you
and your mother's names.

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:20.450
No, you're wrong.

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:22.530
Tony?

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:24.870
I'm not Tony.

00:16:25.520 --> 00:16:28.510
Sure, when I was a showoff little kid,

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:31.020
there were times when I
used the name "Tony"...

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:33.820
But I am not the Tony
you two are looking for.

00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:36.290
My name is Dante.

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:42.530
Don't worry. Just while I'm in
town, I'll play his friend Tony.

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:46.420
So tell me where I can find those ruins.

00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:12.190
Yavalk, Dhimli, Vashatoo...

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:16.700
Wanudune, Shekto, Kaopoke, Umyu...

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:19.800
Yavalk, Dhimli, Vashatoo...

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:23.900
Wanudune, Shekto, Kaopoke, Umyu...

00:17:57.920 --> 00:17:59.170
I can't move!

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:16.920
Tony?!

00:18:31.110 --> 00:18:33.310
This is the devil?

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:35.530
Are you Dante?

00:18:35.530 --> 00:18:37.860
--Huh?
--What if I am?

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:39.200
Tony?

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:43.960
As you're the son of Sparda,
I was wondering what you'd look like.

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:45.940
But it looks like you're still just a kid.

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:48.870
So you'll cut me some slack then?

00:19:00.560 --> 00:19:02.220
Tony... you're...

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:11.640
Get out of here!

00:19:11.640 --> 00:19:13.810
I'm the one this bastard wants!

00:19:13.810 --> 00:19:19.120
So you are! I'm here for your blood, Dante!

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:23.790
Because the moment I have your blood,
the blood of a man born of human and devil,

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:29.550
I can stand lord above the demon world!

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:47.570
20 years ago...

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:51.180
The reason that devil
attacked our town is that it...

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:54.860
wanted you... Tony...

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:11.760
Where's the devil?!

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:14.170
It's all right now. There are no devils.

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:16.000
I saw one!

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:19.140
What am I doing here?

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:23.520
You collapsed at the ruins,
and so Dante brought you here.

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:25.230
Dante?

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:27.140
Where?! Where is he?!

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:28.720
He just left...

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:31.920
Wait! You devil!

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:38.640
Stop it! He's not Tony!

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:42.490
You! If you hadn't been here, none
of those people would have died!

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:44.890
It's all your fault!

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:47.660
That devil destroyed this
town looking for you!

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:48.690
Earnest...

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:51.800
You deceived me and Ms. Margaret!

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:53.830
I'll never forgive you!

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:57.290
Neither will those who died! Do you hear me?!

00:20:57.290 --> 00:21:00.010
Don't you ever come back here again!

00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:04.460
If you ever do, I'll kill you for sure!

00:21:43.290 --> 00:21:49.000
I saw it all. Humans
really are selfish creatures.

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:53.220
They're more horrid than devils.

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:58.200
If you hadn't been there, that town would be
getting devoured by devils right about now

00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:00.510
and there would be an ocean of blood.

00:22:00.940 --> 00:22:03.660
What are you trying to do?

00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:07.870
Something that'll be of use to you.

00:24:02.310 --> 00:24:03.780
I don't mind gambling.

00:24:04.510 --> 00:24:06.800
For one thing, the tension of
those win-or-lose situations

00:24:06.800 --> 00:24:10.040
is similar in some ways to the
feeling I get when I hunt devils.

00:24:10.810 --> 00:24:16.130
In the end, I guess I just can't
be satisfied with a "normal life."

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:20.570
But a person should never
do anything excessively.

00:24:21.110 --> 00:24:24.040
There's nothing more stupid
than gambling oneself into debt.

00:24:24.730 --> 00:24:27.830
Even worse if you go so
far as to lose your life...